            <p>Ocular Ultrasound Techniques in Transverse and Parasagittal Planes. The image displays the clinical application of ultrasound on a patient's eye using a high-frequency linear probe and conductive gel. Panel (a) demonstrates the probe positioned for a transverse plane scan, while panel (b) shows the orientation for a parasagittal plane view. Contributed by Dr. Claire Shelvin</p>
