      <floats-group id="article-79614.s18">
        <fig id="article-79614.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Labeled Diagram of the Human Eye. This cross-section labels the outer structures, including the cornea, sclera, and the uvea, which is composed of the iris, ciliary body, and choroid. The interior is divided into the anterior chamber containing aqueous humour, the posterior chamber, and the large vitreous humour cavity featuring the hyaloid canal. Essential components for vision and focus, such as the pupil, lens, and suspensory ligament of the lens, are shown alongside the sensory retina, macula, fovea, optic disc, retinal blood vessels, and the optic nerve. Contributed by Wikimedia Users Rhcastilhos. And Jmarchn (CC BY-SA 3.0 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en)</p>
          </caption>
